  "instruction": "Please prepare the transaction team's review workbook for the upcoming merger terms discussion.\n\n1. Reconcile the current review population.\n2. Prepare the agreement coding register and identify the review population.\n3. Prepare a summary of the coded terms for the team.\n",
  "design": "This regression retains every question used by the frozen MAUD package. The original labelled source text remains intact. Repeated historical source/term labels are consolidated into one reversible coding register; derived term counts receive conditional consistency credit only. The parallel_coding category is explicit because complete independent source coding remains useful. The generated current and prior review notices carry independent scope facts. The original reference package has richer negotiation/group selection motifs; this normalized spec preserves the three work stages without copying its many-to-one gold rules.\n\nO*NET 31.0, occupation 23-2011.00 (Paralegals and Legal Assistants), Task 23994: \"Prepare, edit, or review legal documents, including legislation, briefs, pleadings, appeals, wills, contracts, and real estate closing statements.\" (local Task Statements.txt, line 5837).\n\nRepair R2: Eligible questions sorted by shortcut_bal_q ascending, then n_labels descending, then question ID ascending only to break an exact tie; take the first 9. Fixed n=16; sample once from records scorable on at least 3 requested questions. Drop questions with fewer than 2 present classes or any present class with fewer than 2 cells; retain at least 5 questions, else fail the seed. No seed replacement or resampling. Screening shortcut_bal_q is the maximum of dedicated, generic-token and five-fold OOF multinomial NB balanced accuracy. The workspace review memo publishes the exact per-record retained question checklist. Label credit remains per-question mean class recall (0.70); scope 0.15, facts 0.10, consistency 0.05.\n\nRepair R3: label credit per question is max(0, (balanced recall - 1/k)/(1 - 1/k)), with k from the complete original codebook. Include-all and ignore-revisions thresholds apply to scope F1, not total reward; each is 0.90. Sampling, questions, scope_exclude_every and weights are unchanged.",
